sview (26.9+stereo3d3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * ORDER 349: the two corrections found in review of the upstream patches
    (gkv311/sview pull requests #186 and #187), carried into this build,
    and one more failure of the same save path that nothing reported.
  * JPS: after saving, the per-file "Swap left and right eyes" is cleared
    only when the saved layout carries the eye order (side by side,
    over/under and row interleaved, in both orders). A red-cyan anaglyph
    has no reversed layout, so its swap was cleared although the file
    could not carry it, and the picture reloaded without the person's
    correction; the swap now stays with the file's per-file choices. The
    per-file input packing is still cleared, since the file now carries
    the layout.
  * JPS: when the section cannot be written (a lossless JPEG has no
    quantization table to place it after), the save stops with the
    file-saving error and the per-file choices are kept. Before, the file
    was left unchanged, no error was shown and the choices were cleared.
  * Frame sequences: the stream's right-first order
    (content_interpretation_type 2, Matroska StereoMode 14) also applies
    when the person chose an input packing. The branch that shows one
    view of a frame sequence runs only then, so its test of the stream's
    order was always false and a right-first sequence shown as one view
    showed the right view; it now shows the left one. A frame sequence
    chosen by the person keeps the stream's eye order too.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

sview (26.9+stereo3d2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * ORDER 312: the edition build has one output, Stereo KWin's. 26.9+stereo3d1
    built and installed sView's six display outputs (anaglyph, interlace, page
    flip, two windows, iZ3D, distorted headset) beside it, and the person could
    pick them, so the player drove displays itself. They are no longer built,
    installed or offered, OpenVR is not used, and a configuration naming
    another output opens on Stereo KWin's.
  * The 3D menu holds Enable 3D, Render resolution per eye and Display
    Configuration (KScreen's module); no display mode, eye separation or
    program-wide JPS eye order. The per-file "Swap left and right eyes" sits
    in the source format menu and is offered only for content shown in 3D.
  * Checkerboard views are compacted from their own samples, no longer
    interpolated; side-by-side quincunx is shown as side by side.
  * JPS: rows are written and read with the "left field first" flag, layouts
    the descriptor cannot describe are not saved as monoscopic, and the
    per-file choices saved into a file are cleared.
  * Right-first frame sequences (content_interpretation_type 2, Matroska
    StereoMode 14) are paired in their own eye order, and the pairs restart
    at the decoded key frame, not at the key frame packet just sent.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

sview (26.9+stereo3d1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add an optional full side-by-side XWayland renderer using
    libstereo-declare 1.6 and the shared one-view place handshake.
  * Decode column, checkerboard and quincunx input layouts explicitly.
  * Keep per-file input packing and eye swap with the recent-file state.
  * Draw controls at zero depth in both views and preserve native samples.
  * Enable the edition renderer in this package and run its tests.

